<title>BELGIUM: EU probes Viag/Goldschmidt, Samsung/AST deals.</title>
<headline>EU probes Viag/Goldschmidt, Samsung/AST deals.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Monday it was opening a routine probe into the following corporate agreements under the European Union's merger rules, which ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions:</p>
<p>-- German diversified group VIAG AG proposed control of Th. Goldschmidt AG, which is active in chemicals, metallurgy, welding and environmental technology (Notified on April 23)</p>
<p>-- Samsung Electronics Co proposed acquisition of the whole of U.S. computer maker AST Research Inc (Notified on April 22)</p>
<p>The Commission has about a month to approve the deal or start a full probe.</p>
</text>
